class.description:
Exposes read-only discovery over the project's FoundryScript files without loading or executing them. Access it through [member FSNamespace.project_scripts] as [code]foundry.project_scripts[/code].
[code]list_scripts_under()[/code] walks a [code]res://[/code] directory and returns one [FSScriptDescriptor] per [code].fs[/code] file, including scripts that fail to parse or index. Filtering policy (name prefixes, annotation matching, excluded directories) stays in runner code; descriptors carry the metadata needed to decide what to run.
Descriptors are built from parser-level indexing via [FSCache] at interface-resolved status. Discovery never runs static initializers, [code]_init[/code], or other user code, and does not print indexing diagnostics to the console. Broken files remain enumerable with [member FSScriptDescriptor.indexed_ok] set to [code]false[/code] and diagnostics available from [method FSScriptDescriptor.get_index_diagnostics].
Example:
[codeblock]
for descriptor in foundry.project_scripts.list_scripts_under("res://tests"):
    if not descriptor.indexed_ok:
        report_broken_file(descriptor.path, descriptor.get_index_diagnostics())
        continue
    if not descriptor.implements_trait(&"my.testlib.Test"):
        continue
    for method in descriptor.get_methods():
        if str(method.name).begins_with("test_"):
            cases.append(TestCase.from_descriptor(descriptor, method))
[/codeblock]
Suites are instantiated later with [method FSScriptDescriptor.load_script].
